  {
    "type": "user",
    "message": {
      "role": "user",
      "content": [
        {
          "tool_use_id": "toolu_019kHbq64PGeRtZunGBSW2C9",
          "type": "tool_result",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Some of factorio's settings are not stored in any config file on this server \u2014 they are read from the environment when the game starts, and the only place an instance can set them is .grizzly/env, at the top of the data directory. It is always there, often empty. Don't go looking for a config file for these: there isn't one, and searching for it is time spent on something that cannot be found.\n\nExactly these settings do anything in that file, and the rest are ignored: LOAD_LATEST_SAVE and SAVE_NAME. A line naming anything else is dropped when the game launches, so the change will look like it worked and won't have.\n\nRead the file first to see what's already set, then change it like any other config file \u2014 one setting at a time \u2014 and restart to apply it. That restart self-guards: if the game refuses a value and won't start, the previous version of the file is restored and the server restarted automatically, and you'll be told. So a value you're unsure of is worth trying rather than talking around; afterwards, read_logs to confirm it took rather than assuming.\n\nThere is no supported way to install mods on factorio through this bot \u2014 no registry is wired up for it, so there is nothing to search and nothing to write. Say so plainly. Don't improvise an install by hand through the file tools: anything put there that way is outside everything that would otherwise check it and put it back. If someone wants mods on this game, escalate it as a feature request."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "parent_tool_use_id": null,
    "session_id": "c5540fc2-48b9-4f73-b60b-2a3ad4b0a6b9",
    "uuid": "10b4d2d4-062f-4383-8d59-295ddadc5d0c",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-02T22:18:46.178Z",
    "tool_use_result": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Some of factorio's settings are not stored in any config file on this server \u2014 they are read from the environment when the game starts, and the only place an instance can set them is .grizzly/env, at the top of the data directory. It is always there, often empty. Don't go looking for a config file for these: there isn't one, and searching for it is time spent on something that cannot be found.\n\nExactly these settings do anything in that file, and the rest are ignored: LOAD_LATEST_SAVE and SAVE_NAME. A line naming anything else is dropped when the game launches, so the change will look like it worked and won't have.\n\nRead the file first to see what's already set, then change it like any other config file \u2014 one setting at a time \u2014 and restart to apply it. That restart self-guards: if the game refuses a value and won't start, the previous version of the file is restored and the server restarted automatically, and you'll be told. So a value you're unsure of is worth trying rather than talking around; afterwards, read_logs to confirm it took rather than assuming.\n\nThere is no supported way to install mods on factorio through this bot \u2014 no registry is wired up for it, so there is nothing to search and nothing to write. Say so plainly. Don't improvise an install by hand through the file tools: anything put there that way is outside everything that would otherwise check it and put it back. If someone wants mods on this game, escalate it as a feature request."
      }
    ],
